  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing primary health care services in Kirkuk, Ninawa and Salahaddin governorates</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving access to essential health care services for crisis-affected populations (out of camps IDPs and vulnerable returnees) in Ninawa, Diyala, and Salahaddin governorates aiming to reduce avoidable morbidity and mortality with improving access to dignified and safe specialized referral services for people in need of humanitarian assistance in the target locations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project activities will target out-of-camp IDPs and vulnerable returnees living in the underserved and high-severity districts in Diyala, Ninawa, and Salahaddin governorate</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a consortium project that includes two national NGOs, Dary Human organization (the consortium lead) and AAF. one international NGO, CORDAID, the consortium project aims to provide primary and reproductive health care services for out of camps IDPs and returnees in Diyala, Ninawa and Salahaddin governorates. 

The intervention will provide continuation of ongoing life-saving assistance while ensuring access to essential and quality primary and reproductive health care services for IDPs and returnees&#x2019; families in a manner that is accountable, conflict-sensitive, and supports the government&apos;s responsibility as the first responder.</narrative>
  </description>
